RF.put("questb:b52",{"8692":{"id":8692,"t":"Cloak of Unending Life","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Qiraji Regal Drape, 2 Vermillion Idols, 5 Silver Scarabs and 5 Bone Scarabs to Keyl Swiftclaw in Silithus. You must also obtain Revered reputation with Cenarion Circle to complete this quest.\nQiraji Regal Drape General Rajaxx 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Kurinnaxx 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Ayamiss the Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Buru the Gorger 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj\n2 Vermillion Idol Flesh Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Drone 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Collector 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Soldier 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 4 more\n5 Bone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Silver Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 21000 reputation with Cenarion Circle","desc":"I'm glad to hear you're aiding us in our attack on Ahn'Qiraj, ‹name›. I can make you a protective item that'll be of assistance in the fight against our enemy, ‹class›.\nI shall need a Qiraji drape, which I'll resize for you of course. I'll also need idols and scarabs which I'll use to create a suitable clasp.\nI promise you won't be disappointed.","rew":"You will receive:\nCloak of Unending Life\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Did you bring the materials for the cloak, ‹name›?","done":"Ah yes... this drape is immaculate.\nTake this cloak, ‹name›. May it protect you from the foul magic of the Qiraji.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.8,"y":39.5,"n":"Keyl Swiftclaw","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8852":{"id":8852,"t":"Ten Signets for War Supplies","lv":29,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Horde Commendation Signet","rew":"You will receive:\nAhn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":29.8,"y":67.3,"n":"Warlord Gorchuk","s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8532":{"id":8532,"t":"The Horde Needs Copper Bars!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 54.","obj":"Bring 20 Copper Bars to Miner Cromwell at the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar.\n20 Copper Bar","desc":"So glad that you've decided to help out here. Not everyone would, so I need to make sure you understand what it is that I need. Copper bars, not copper ore. We don't have the time or people to do all of the smelting ourselves, so if you would be so kind as to take care of that, your efforts will be duly noted. Is that something that you can handle, ‹class›?","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Horde Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"I hope that's the twenty copper bars you have there with you, ‹class›.","done":"These bars will do, and thanks for not shining them. No sense in making them pretty when they're going to be mangled for whatever materiel needs to be built for the war. I'll take care of putting them on the stacks, and I'll make sure that they are put to proper use. Speak to me again if you're interested in bringing in another twenty.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":31.6,"y":66.7,"n":"Miner Cromwell","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8612":{"id":8612,"t":"The Horde Needs More Lean Wolf Steaks!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 Lean Wolf Steaks to Bloodguard Rawtar at the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar.\n20 Lean Wolf Steak","desc":"As you can see, ‹class›, we still need to pack away more food for the soldiers. I don't know if you've ever been in a war before, but once you get past the initial shock of the battlefield, you can get pretty hungry. You did a good job last time, so I expect that you'll do as well, if not a little quicker, in getting me another stack of those lean wolf steaks.","rew":"You will receive:\nHorde Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":28.8,"y":67.4,"n":"Bloodguard Rawtar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"5892":{"id":5892,"t":"Irondeep Supplies","lv":55,"min":51,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 55 instead of 60. Pays 40s instead of 0.","obj":"Bring 10 Irondeep Supplies to the Alliance Quartermaster in Dun Baldar.\n10 Irondeep Supplies Irondeep Supplies in Alterac Valley","desc":"Before the fighting started, we stored supplies for Dun Baldar in the Irondeep mine. The troggs that surfaced there weren't much of a problem when we had spare troops to guard the mine, but now that we're fighting with the Horde we can't maintain control of Irondeep.\nWe need the supplies in Irondeep, ‹name›. Enter the mine and bring me a load of them.","rew":"Money: 40 0 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper\n+25 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Do you have the supplies, ‹name›? We can never have enough!","done":"Well done! I'll put these supplies to good use! Thanks, ‹name›!\nStart Stormpike Quartermaster Alterac Valley End Stormpike Quartermaster Alterac Valley Level 55 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 53 58 Side Alliance Type PvP Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 5892","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"7172":{"id":7172,"t":"The Eye of Command","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Stormpike Insignia Rank 5","desc":"It is good to see you again, ‹class›. I had not expected you to return. Alas, you have proven yourself a brave and honorable soldier of the Frostwolf.\nYour time has come again, ‹name›. You have earned a new ranking and as such, a new insignia denoting this rise in stature.\nPresent your insignia.","rew":"You will receive:\nStormpike Insignia Rank 6\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Ironforge\n+200 reputation with Stormpike Guard","back":"Let them hear your voice, Commander ‹name›! Let them know fear. Show them what power the Stormpike holds in their rank!\nPresent your insignia.","done":"It is you who must lead our troops to victory, Commander! The soldiers are under your command. They will follow your direct orders. Lead them.... Crush the Frostwolf.","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":39.5,"y":81.2,"n":"Lieutenant Haggerdin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-valley"]},"1012":{"id":1012,"t":"Insane Druids","lv":32,"min":24,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Uthil's Cudgel, Mavoris's Warstaff.","obj":"Kill the druids: Taneel Darkwood, Uthil Mooncall, Mavoris Cloudsbreak; then return to Kayneth Stillwind in Forest Song.\nTaneel Darkwood slain\nUthil Mooncall slain\nMavoris Cloudsbreak slain","desc":"When I struggled with the Forsaken's poisons, I had a vision. I had a vision of the druids in the Dor'danil Barrow Den, poisoned... murdered by the undead! They are now errant ghosts, severed from their bodies and driven mad.\nSo that the druids' spirits might some day find peace, you must enter the Dor'danil Barrow Den and destroy its once great leaders: Taneel Darkwood, Uthil Mooncall and Mavoris Cloudsbreak.\nDo this, then return to me.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nEmil's Brand Uthil's Cudgel Mavoris's Warstaff\nNew in Forever: Uthil's Cudgel, Mavoris's Warstaff.\nExperience: 3,200\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","back":"The anguish of the Dor'danil druids still haunt my dreams, ‹name›. You must destroy their leaders!","done":"I felt the anguish of the Dor'danil Barrows lessen, and knew you had completed your task.\nIt was grim work you did, ‹name›, for the spirits you destroyed were merely victims of the Forsaken's evil. But with their destruction, let us hope the other maddened spirits find peace.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":85.2,"y":44.7,"n":"Kayneth Stillwind","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"692":{"id":692,"t":"The Lost Fragments","lv":41,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Torn Scroll Fragment, the Crumpled Scroll Fragment and the Singed Scroll Fragment to Theldurin the Lost.\nTorn Scroll Fragment Enraged Rock Elemental 33 %\nCrumpled Scroll Fragment Enraged Rock Elemental 33 %\nSinged Scroll Fragment Enraged Rock Elemental 33 %","desc":"The Scroll of Myzrael...the Scroll of Myzrael?! You don't want that! Its magic can pull Myzrael to the surface world and if you do that, we are in trouble!\nOr...maybe it's too late. Maybe she already is free. Maybe she's just gathering strength before unleashing herself upon us. If so, then you'll NEED the scroll!\n...too bad it's destroyed. Enraged elementals stole it and tore it up and now fight over the fragments.\nBut if you can gather those fragments, maybe we can fix it...","rew":"Experience: 3,300","back":"Did you find those fragments?!?! You'll need the Scroll of Myzrael if you want to trap her again, before it's too late!","done":"Ah, you found them! Good work, ‹name›! These might be the only chance we have against the evil of Myzrael!\nJust let me find my scrap-ratchet and see if I can re-attach these fragments...","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":51.4,"y":76.9,"n":"Theldurin the Lost","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"4132":{"id":4132,"t":"Operation: Death to Angerforge","lv":58,"min":52,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Blackrock Depths and slay General Angerforge! Return to Warlord Goretooth when the task is complete.\nGeneral Angerforge slain","desc":"You have done an exemplary job, ‹name›. It is now time to send you on your last mission.\nGeneral Angerforge, the Dark Iron responsible for coordinating the attacks on the 109th division of the K.E.F. and the mass slaughter of our forces must be brought to justice.\nThis will undoubtedly be your most grueling mission, but should you succeed, you will be richly rewarded.","rew":"You will receive:\nConqueror's Medallion\nMoney: 2 65 2 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 7,750\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Has the Butcher of Blackrock been disposed of?","done":"Finally! The villain been brought to justice! You are a remarkable individual, ‹name›. Wear this medallion as a symbol of your stalwart dedication to the Horde and the K.E.F.","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":5.8,"y":47.5,"n":"Warlord Goretooth","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"2772":{"id":2772,"t":"The World At Your Feet","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring two Heavy Mithril Boots and one Ornate Mithril Pants to Trenton Lighthammer.\n2 Heavy Mithril Boots\nOrnate Mithril Pants","desc":"At last year's All-Valley Blacksmithing Championship, all those who watched saw my leg get swept from under me by a cowardly dog from the Venture Co. Foundry. What they didn't know, however, was the reason I was able to continue and ultimately win the tournament: That's right, ornate mithril boots!\nI will need to learn how to craft ornate mithril pants for this year's tournament, however, as a Venture Co. shredder is an entrant! Teach me the way of the pants and learn the way of the boot!","rew":"You will learn: Ornate Mithril Boots\nExperience: 3,900","back":"Have you completed the crafting of the items, ‹name›?","done":"The world will be at your feet, ‹name›! Let them all come at your legs, for you are now unsweepable!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":51.4,"y":28.8,"n":"Trenton Lighthammer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"7652":{"id":7652,"t":"A Blue Light Bargain","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","done":"Aright, mister, I got a hot deal for ya.\nI'm lookin' to offload some of these here Imperial plate armor recipes and need someone willing to take on the burden. All I want in exchange is some thorium bars. Sound good?","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":51.4,"y":28.7,"n":"Derotain Mudsipper","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"97972":{"id":97972,"t":"Camping 101 tailoring","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Taleen Shimmerthread in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your tailoring skill to 20","desc":"Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.\nI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Rallying Banner. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":41.6,"y":44.8,"n":"Raan Wildwind","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":44.8,"y":44.2,"n":"Taleen Shimmerthread","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"6612":{"id":6612,"t":"I Know A Guy...","lv":45,"min":35,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Gadgetzan in the Tanaris desert and speak with Dirge Quikcleave about advancing your cooking career.","desc":"I can tell by yer cooking spoon that ye know what yer doin'. Unfortunately, I can't teach ya nothin'.\nLuckily fer ye, I know a guy. He's a goblin and probably the best cook on Kalimdor.\nAyep, that's the bad news, lad/missy - ye got to travel to Kalimdor. Git to Gadgetzan and find Dirge Quikcleave. He'll set ya straight.","rew":"Experience: 975","done":"<Dirge spits out leather.>\nPfftey...\n<Dirge hacks loudly.>\nWhat? I'll have you know that leather is surprisingly high in protein and low in carbohydrates, ‹race›.\nDun Morogh Tanaris","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":60.7,"y":26.9,"n":"Daryl Riknussun","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.6,"y":28.1,"n":"Dirge Quikcleave","e":1}],"cats":["cooking"]},"94292":{"id":94292,"t":"Craftsmans writ comfortable leather hat","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Comfortable Leather Hat\nComfortable Leather Hat","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Comfortable Leather Hat, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Comfortable Leather Hat Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94292","cats":["crafting"]},"94212":{"id":94212,"t":"Craftsmans writ elixir of wisdom","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Elixir of Wisdom\nElixir of Wisdom","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Elixir of Wisdom, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"Come, warm yourself by the fire.","done":"I will admit, I expected the treacherous winds of the highlands to tear that letter to shreds. I had not imagined that someone would see my humble request, let alone deliver it straight to me.\nYour efforts are kind and admirable, ‹race›. I will use this to aid my meditation.\nFeel free to stay and share a tale or two of your travels. I enjoy the company.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":48.6,"y":55.7,"n":"Muggol Breezebeard","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"7892":{"id":7892,"t":"Big Black Mace","lv":60,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Big Black Mace","rew":"You will receive:\n12 Darkmoon Faire Prize Ticket\n+100 reputation with Darkmoon Faire","back":"For my act as the strongest woman alive, I plan to accept items from the audience and smash them with a big, black mace!\nCan you make me a big black mace, ‹name›?","done":"Thanks much, ‹name›. Here's your Darkmoon Faire tickets!\nMulgore Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":38.6,"y":46.4,"n":"Kerri Hicks","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":40.5,"y":69.9,"n":"Kerri Hicks","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"6132":{"id":6132,"t":"Get Me Out of Here!","lv":39,"min":34,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Escort Melizza Brimbuzzle, then speak with Hornizz Brimbuzzle at the Kodo Graveyard in Desolace.","desc":"Get me out of here!\nI came up to the Valley of Spears to talk to the Maraudines. I thought I could do a little business with them... but they don't want to talk! I think they want to eat me!\nGet me out of here and my brother Hornizz will pay you big! He's at our camp next to the kodo graveyard, to the east.\nLet's hurry, ‹name›. Not two minutes ago I heard some centaurs talking about getting wood for their cookpot...","rew":"Money: 45 0 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,250","back":"Have you seen my sister Melizza? She's always on the go, which gets her into trouble all the time.","done":"My sister Melizza said you'd be coming. Thanks a lot for getting her out of the jam she was in; it's too bad that she's already probably found herself in a new one!","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":33.9,"y":53.5,"n":"Melizza Brimbuzzle","s":1},{"z":"Desolace","x":47.8,"y":61.8,"n":"Hornizz Brimbuzzle","e":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"7492":{"id":7492,"t":"Camp Mojache","lv":57,"min":54,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Talo Thornhoof at Camp Mojache in Feralas.","desc":"Talo Thornhoof, a Tauren elder in Feralas, sends a request for aid. He offered few details, but he did say that he needs agents for a matter both delicate... and dire.\nServe the Horde, ‹name›. Go to Camp Mojache in Feralas and speak with Talo.","rew":"Experience: 1,500","done":"Ah, it is good to see a ‹class› heed my summons. I have need of your services, ‹name›, and fear they will take you down a dangerous path...\nA path into Dire Maul.\nOrgrimmar Feralas","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":48.2,"y":66.1,"n":"Warcaller Gorlach","s":1},{"z":"Feralas","x":76.2,"y":43.8,"n":"Talo Thornhoof","e":1}],"cats":["dire-maul"]},"1252":{"id":1252,"t":"Lieutenant Paval Reethe","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Reethe's Badge to Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore.\nReethe's Badge\nProvided: Reethe's Badge","desc":"A glint of light on the ground catches your eye from underneath the rubble. Brushing away debris and ash caked onto the object reveals the insignia of a gold anchor on white enameled on the surface: the sign of Theramore.\nUnderneath the anchor is embossed the name \"Lieutenant Paval Reethe\".","rew":"Experience: 775","back":"Have you found anything of interest at the Shady Rest Inn?","done":"It's never good news when a guard's badge is brought to me.\nSometimes it's a man or woman who's fallen in battle, and I'm left to bring the news to the grieving family. Other times we never find out what happened to them. And other times it's even worse than that.","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":29.8,"y":48.2,"n":"Theramore Guard Badge","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":68.2,"y":48.6,"n":"Captain Garran Vimes","e":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"1172":{"id":1172,"t":"The Brood of Onyxia","lv":45,"min":38,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Draz'Zilb in Brackenwall Village wants you to destroy 5 Eggs of Onyxia.\nEgg of Onyxia destroyed : 0/ 5","desc":"Onyxia's brood has been scattered across the Dragonmurk. It is imperative that no more whelps be permitted to hatch.\nMake haste to Wyrmbog in the south of Dustwallow Marsh. Surely, she has made her lair there. Track down the evil dragon's eggs and destroy them.\nWe will never reclaim Stonemaul Village if the surrounding area remains a breeding ground.\nAs for Mok'Morokk... I have other plans for the sod.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nEncarmine Boots Boots of Zua'tec\nExperience: 4,850","back":"You must hurry to the Dragonmurk, ‹name›. With Onyxia's eggs riddled around the Wyrmbog, we face overwhelming numbers unless something is done quickly.\nDestroy her eggs! Don't let the black dragon plague spread across our homeland!","done":"Splendid! It will be sometime before Onyxia can produce more eggs.\nOn behalf of my people, I thank you, ‹name›.\nI have asked much of you so far. Perhaps you can do the Stonemaul Clan one last service.\nMok'Morokk is not fit to lead us. Tharg would make an excellent leader but is hindered by his injuries and age. Drive Mok'Morokk from this place by force. Only then can we appoint a new leader to return us to our proper home in the south.","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":37.2,"y":33.1,"n":"Draz'Zilb","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"91732":{"id":91732,"t":"Good steel","lv":10,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 4 Mining Tools from Jasperlode Mine, then return to Hagar Lowe in Eastvale Logging Camp.\n4 Mining Tools","desc":"Good steel is in short supply after the war, and our tools have suffered for it. The Jasperlode miners used finely-crafted picks, and I imagine some of them are still there in the depths of the mine. Could you retrieve some for me, and I'll see if I can repurpose the steel?","rew":"Money: 2 50 0 gold, 2 silver, 50 copper Experience: 625\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Have you been to the mine yet?","done":"Oh, very nice. Do you see that shine? Truly, they don't make them like they used to.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":82.4,"y":63.8,"n":"Hagar Lowe","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"52":{"id":52,"t":"Protect the Frontier","lv":10,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 8 Prowlers and 5 Young Forest Bears, and then return to Guard Thomas at the east Elwynn bridge.\nProwler slain : 0/ 8\nYoung Forest Bear slain : 0/ 5","desc":"Hail, ‹name›. Wild animals are growing more and more aggressive the farther we get from Goldshire, and the Eastvale Logging Camp suffers nearly constant attacks from wolves and bears!\nWe could use your help out here.","rew":"You will receive:\n2 Lesser Healing Potion\nMoney: 2 50 0 gold, 2 silver, 50 copper Experience: 625\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Have you killed those wolves and bears?","done":"Thanks a lot for the help, ‹name›. Something in the forest must be making these animals so bold.\nWhatever it is, I hope it stays there.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":74,"y":72.2,"n":"Guard Thomas","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"7732":{"id":7732,"t":"Zukk'ash Report","lv":48,"min":39,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the Camp Mojache Zukk'ash Report to Zilzibin Drumlore. He resides in the Drag of Orgrimmar.\nCamp Mojache Zukk'ash Report\nProvided: Camp Mojache Zukk'ash Report","desc":"You've done doubly well in addressing the threat that the Zukk'ash insects pose to Camp Mojache. The threat these things pose is far from over, and I'd like to ask you for one last task on behalf of the Horde.\nThis is a document that details all the information we have learned about these Zukk'ash insects. I want you to deliver it to Zilzibin Drumlore in the Drag of Orgrimmar. He's an expert on alien creatures like these; I hope he can do something with the lore we've obtained.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nRing of Subtlety Emerald Peak Spaulders\nExperience: 4,400\n+50 reputation with Horde","back":"Greetings friend... you look as though you are on urgent business. Is there something I can help you with?","done":"Ah, I've been expecting this. These creatures you faced... they are an ancient threat that the Horde continues to choose to ignore. Hadoken was wise to bring this - and you - to me.\nThe Zukk'ash are nothing more than creatures called the silithid. Some would think that they are a mindless nuisance, but let me assure you - they are a far, far worse threat than anything the Alliance could muster.\nIf you're willing and strong enough, I could use your aid in bringing this threat to light.\nFeralas Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":74.9,"y":42.5,"n":"Hadoken Swiftstrider","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":56.3,"y":46.7,"n":"Zilzibin Drumlore","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"532":{"id":532,"t":"Battle of Hillsbrad","lv":26,"min":19,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Magistrate Burnside and 4 Hillsbrad Councilmen. Destroy the Hillsbrad Proclamation. Steal the Hillsbrad Town Registry. Report back to Darthalia in Tarren Mill afterwards.\nHillsbrad Town Registry Hillsbrad Town Registry\nMagistrate Burnside slain\nHillsbrad Councilman slain : 0/ 4\nHillsbrad Proclamation destroyed","desc":"The town of Hillsbrad is in disarray and we believe it will soon fall. We must, however, persist in our ruthlessness until the human scum are wiped from the foothills for eternity.\nDespite their overwhelming losses, the humans rally around their leadership and keep fighting. We must eliminate their leader, Magistrate Burnside, as well as the town council. Destroy their revered political document as well, the Hillsbrad Proclamation. And while you're at it, steal the town registry.","rew":"Money: 20 0 gold, 20 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,100\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"What news have you?","done":"News of your glories in Hillsbrad traveled fast. You have done well, ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":62.3,"y":20.5,"n":"High Executor Darthalia","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"3092":{"id":3092,"t":"Etched Note","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 40 experience instead of 50, 0.8 times as much.","obj":"Read the Etched Note and speak to Lanka Farshot in Red Cloud Mesa.\nEtched Note\nProvided: Etched Note","desc":"Just a moment ago a messenger was looking for you, ‹name›. I believe she was sent by the hunter trainer Lanka. If this note is from Lanka, I wouldn't take long in reading it's contents.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Welcome to Camp Narache, ‹name›. I hear good things about you. Your bloodline is strong, and many of the elders consider you skilled already. But that we will test.\nThe plains of Mulgore will be your home for sometime--you should do your best to learn it very well. One day you will travel to unfamilar lands to master greater skills. You must be ready.","done":"And it is my job to make sure you are prepared by teaching you the basics of our profession--how to tame your pet, how to fire your rifle, and many other skills that will become necessary.\nHunters are a strong part of our tradition and history, ‹name›. You would do well to remember how important you are to the tribe. You will be respected and revered if you serve our people well.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":44.5,"y":77.5,"n":"Grull Hawkwind","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":44,"y":76.4,"n":"Lanka Farshot","e":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"7812":{"id":7812,"t":"Additional Runecloth","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"20 Runecloth Stormwind Royal Guard , Honor Guard , Skullsplitter Speaker in Zul'Gurub , General Marcus Jonathan 85.7 % and 4 more","back":"Greetings once again, ‹name›! Our need for runecloth is constant, and we can always use additional resources if you are willing to part with them. For an additional stack of twenty runecloth, I will make sure that you are recognized for your continuing efforts on behalf of the Gnomeregan Exiles.\nWhenever you are ready to hand in the stack of runecloth, I'll accept it.","done":"‹name› - without heroes like you working on behalf of the gnomes, we'd surely suffer. Thank you for your continued efforts!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63,"y":28.8,"n":"Bubulo Acerbus","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"8932":{"id":8932,"t":"Just Compensation","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Magister's Belt and a set of Magister's Gloves to Deliana in Ironforge.\nMagister's Belt Crimson Battle Mage 2.6 % , Smolderthorn Mystic 2.2 % , Crimson Sorcerer 1.9 % in Stratholme , Scholomance Adept 1.6 % in Scholomance and 3 more\nMagister's Gloves Doctor Theolen Krastinov 14 % in Scholomance , Scholomance Adept 4.6 % in Scholomance","desc":"You kept your word and brought the device built by Mux. I believe a reward is in order if I'm to keep you interested in saving my skin. Bring me an ordinary belt and a set of gloves that you wish to upgrade.","rew":"You will receive:\nSorcerer's Belt Sorcerer's Gloves\nExperience: 9,950","back":"You're ready to perform the trade?","done":"You've kept your end of the bargain, I shall keep mine.\nJust remember that I'm holding on to the best pieces until your work is finished.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"2852":{"id":2852,"t":"Wild Leather Leggings","lv":45,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 2 Turtle Scale Helms, 2 Turtle Scale Bracers, and 2 Wildvines to Pratt McGrubben in Feathermoon Stronghold.\n2 Turtle Scale Helm\n2 Turtle Scale Bracers\n2 Wildvine Retherokk the Berserker 80.6 % , Zul'arek Hatefowler 65.1 % , Purple Lotus 10 % , Vilebranch Aman'zasi Guard 9.5 % and 4 more","desc":"With the basics down, you are ready to master more complex fare, ‹name›. Wild Leather leggings are some of the sturdiest and powerful leather gear around. The waist, thighs, calves, and the vitals - all are given tremendous protection. Coupled with the enhancement that the wildvine provides, adventurers who own it will thank you each time they see you.\nFor this pattern, I need an order of two Turtle Scale helms, two Turtle Scale bracers, and two wildvines filled.","rew":"You will receive:\nPattern: Wild Leather Leggings\nExperience: 2,900","back":"Do you have the Turtle Scale bracers and helms ready? Don't forget the two wildvines I need!\nBy now, you're starting to realize the potential power that lies in Wild Leather armor. An armor that has no boundaries in application is nearly invaluable to a leatherworker. The limits are only in the quantities of resources to make the items - not the quality of the finished products!","done":"Again, you've filled an order without flaw. Perhaps some day I will come to YOU seeking knowledge, eh ‹name›?\nHere is the pattern for the leggings, along with my thanks. Commit this lore to your knowledge, and let your finished products tap into your impressive skills!","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":30.6,"y":42.7,"n":"Pratt McGrubben","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["leatherworking"]},"9332":{"id":9332,"t":"Stealing Darnassus's Flame","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 70s instead of 0. Gives 4,950 experience instead of 5,000, 0.99 times as much.","obj":"Return the Flame of Darnassus to the Festival Talespinner.\nFlame of Darnassus\nProvided: Flame of Darnassus","desc":"This flame, stolen from the shores of Teldrassil, floods you with warmth. This raw power is foreign to you, but the Talespinner might know more...","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\n10 Elderberry Pie 10 Fire-toasted Bun 10 Midsummer Sausage 10 Toasted Smorc\nYou will also receive:\n20 Burning Blossom\nMoney: 70 0 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,950","back":"You're practically glowing, ‹race›. What do you have there?","done":"This fire aches of ancient sorrow, ‹name›. You pulled this from the roots of Teldrassil, you say? Fascinating! Here is a reward for your skill. Return to me should you find anything else like this; I may have a use for it.\nThunder Bluff Orgrimmar Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":21.5,"y":27.2,"n":"Festival Talespinner","e":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":42.8,"y":34.9,"n":"Festival Talespinner","e":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.9,"y":73.1,"n":"Festival Talespinner","e":1}],"cats":["midsummer"]},"772":{"id":772,"t":"Rite of Vision","lv":7,"min":3,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Consume the Water of the Seers in front of the tribal fire in Bloodhoof Village and follow the vision once it appears.\nProvided: Water of the Seers","desc":"I now present you with the Water of the Seers.\nWhen you are ready, consume the waters near the tribal fire. Once you have ingested the holy waters, it will take a few moments before the vision materializes before the fire.\nAt that point, it is up to you to follow it to your destiny....","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nRainwalker Boots Sun-beaten Cloak\nExperience: 480\n+75 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"Be not afraid, ‹name›. You have successfully passed the Rite of Vision.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.9,"y":61.2,"n":"Zarlman Two-Moons","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":34.3,"y":43.3,"n":"Seer Wiserunner","e":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9092":{"id":9092,"t":"Dreamwalker Girdle","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Rayne at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make a Dreamwalker Girdle if you bring her the following: 1 Desecrated Girdle, 8 Wartorn Leather Scraps, 3 Mooncloth and 2 Cured Rugged Hides.\nDesecrated Girdle Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Heigan the Unclean 0 % in Naxxramas , Noth the Plaguebringer 0 % in Naxxramas\n8 Wartorn Leather Scrap Skeletal Steed 26.1 % in Naxxramas , Necro Knight Guardian 26.1 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 24.5 % in Naxxramas , Stoneskin Gargoyle 24.1 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n3 Mooncloth\n2 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"Many heroes fell in the last war and many continue to perish at the hands of the Scourge to this day. From the corpses of the fallen, the armor is stripped and taken back to Naxxramas to be used for unknown purposes.\nRecover the desecrated armor and wartorn armor scraps and supply to me the other material components I require and I will craft Dreamwalker armor.","rew":"You will receive:\nDreamwalker Girdle\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"The material cost is high, but soon forgotten.","done":"Your Dreamwalker Girdle is ready, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.4,"y":49.3,"n":"Rayne","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"9012":{"id":9012,"t":"Saving the Best for Last","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Give Mokvar your Dreadmist Mask and Dreadmist Robe.\nDreadmist Mask Darkmaster Gandling 0 %\nDreadmist Robe General Drakkisath 0 %","desc":"A truly amazing story, ‹name›! You have my thanks, and the heartfelt gratitude of all who were involved, I can assure you. Through your efforts we are delivered from the mistakes of our past.\nAs to your reward, I believe I have a few things that you have definitely earned and will truly enjoy.","rew":"You will receive:\nDeathmist Mask Deathmist Robe\nExperience: 1,650","back":"As per our deal, are you ready to hand over your Dreadmist pieces in exchange for your new Deathmist Mask and Robe?","done":"I will truly miss you, ‹name›. There is a debt that I owe you, which I may never be able to repay.\nEnjoy your new head and chest armor. May it protect you for a long time to come, and help you to achieve even greater honor!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"1652":{"id":1652,"t":"The Tome of Valor","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Duthorian Rall in Stormwind.","desc":"Please, return to Duthorian and let him know that I'm safe for now. I have you and the Church to thank for that.\nHe'll send word to Ironforge to let my Jordan know that he has nothing to fear.\nOh, how I miss my husband. I can't wait till he returns.","rew":"You will receive:\nBastion of Stormwind\nYou will learn: Sense Undead\nExperience: 2,550","done":"So, we meet again, ‹name›, and you are in high spirits, I see.\nThe Stilwell home will be safe for another day, and from your story I see that there was no shortage of danger to be found. Well done.\nDaphne and Jordan have helped the Church greatly, and having you protect their property--and their very lives--was the least we could do for them.\nFor your valor, you will be rewarded.\nWestfall Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":41.7,"y":89.2,"n":"Daphne Stilwell","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":50.5,"y":47.5,"n":"Duthorian Rall","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"5652":{"id":5652,"t":"Hex of Weakness","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Ur'kyo in Orgrimmar.","desc":"I sent here to make sure that you not wander too far from home, ‹name›. They send me to make sure you return home because Ur'kyo, greatest of our priests, wish to speak to you. You go there. You got to the Valley of Spirits in the orc city and you speak to Ur'kyo. He wait for you now.","rew":"You will learn: Hex of Weakness","done":"You would do well to pay heed to this lesson, young one. The Hex of Weakness will be a great boon to you in battle. Later I will have tests for you to further yourself and prove your worth to the tribe.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":35.6,"y":87.8,"n":"Ur'kyo","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"8772":{"id":8772,"t":"Target: Hive'Zora Waywatchers","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay 30 Hive'Zora Waywatchers and report back to Commander Mar'alith at Cenarion Hold in Silithus. You must also bring Combat Task Briefing VI in order to complete this quest.\nCombat Task Briefing VI\nHive'Zora Waywatcher slain : 0/ 30\nProvided: Combat Task Briefing VI","desc":"Reinforcements have been called on to join the assault on Hive'Zora. You have been selected to target Hive'Zora waywatchers. Report back to Commander Mar'alith after completing your task.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Combat Badge\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"You have something to tell me, ‹class›?","done":"Excellent work, ‹name›. Your part in the attack on Hive'Zora has been noted.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.2,"y":34.2,"n":"Commander Mar'alith","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"452":{"id":452,"t":"Pyrewood Ambush","lv":15,"min":12,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 14s instead of 7s.","obj":"Help Deathstalker Faerleia kill the Pyrewood Council.","desc":"You got here just in the nick of time, ‹name›!\nThe Pyrewood Council will be returning any moment. Arugal has other matters to tend to in the keep. He uses the Council as mere puppets to keep the mindless minions of Pyrewood under his control. But I believe that without the guidance of the Pyrewood Council, the sons of Arugal will turn against their master.\nI cannot handle them all by myself. I need you to help me. Together we can lay waste to the Council for Lady Sylvanas.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFaerleia's Shield Stretched Leather Trousers Mystic Shawl\nMoney: 14 0 gold, 14 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,350\n+150 reputation with Undercity","done":"You fought like a true disciple of the Dark Lady, ‹name›. With the council dead, perhaps we can gain control of this town once and for all and drive Arugal from Shadowfang Keep. I salute you!","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":46.5,"y":74.4,"n":"Deathstalker Faerleia","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"79092":{"id":79092,"t":"Archmage theocritus research journal","lv":20,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Archmage Theocritus' Research Journal","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 1 25 0 gold, 1 silver, 25 copper Experience: 160","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nArchmage Theocritus' Research Journal (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.8,"y":80.2,"n":"Garion Wendell","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.6,"y":33,"n":"Owen Thadd","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"1092":{"id":1092,"t":"Gerenzo's Orders","lv":22,"min":17,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the Unidentified Ore to Ziz Fizziks in the Stonetalon Mountains.\nUnidentified Ore\nProvided: Unidentified Ore","desc":"I guess I'd better think about getting out of here, also. It won't take long for word of what happened here to spread to the higher ups, and I'm sure they wouldn't take too kindly to meeting me again.\nI'll sneak out and meet with Ziz. Hopefully, he'll be able to find me a new job!\nI'll try and clean up this mess a little, but you should take the ore sample to Ziz right away. He told me that he'd set up camp somewhere on the western side of Windshear Crag. Good luck.","rew":"You will receive:\nDredge Boots\nExperience: 1,300\n+75 reputation with Ratchet","back":"Something I can help you with?","done":"Ahhh, I knew that I did the right thing by telling Piznik to stay behind. I'm sure the engineers in Undermine will be most interested to look at this...\nOf course I'll want to keep a little piece for myself, but what they don't know won't hurt them, yes?","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":71.9,"y":60,"n":"Piznik","s":1},{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":59,"y":62.6,"n":"Ziz Fizziks","e":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"212":{"id":212,"t":"A Meal Served Cold","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill a Cold Eye Basilisk, get a Chilled Basilisk Haunch, and return it to Angus Stern in the Blue Recluse.\nChilled Basilisk Haunch Cold Eye Basilisk","desc":"One of my most famous dishes is Chilled Basilisk in Lime Vinaigrette. But the problem is... the meat is impossible to keep fresh, and I must serve the dish tonight for a noble's birthday!\nSo if you can bring me a Chilled Basilisk Haunch from a freshly-killed Cold Eye Basilisk, quickly, then I will owe you a king's feast!\nCold Eye Basilisks are known to roam along the beach dunes of northwestern Stranglethorn, so you have much traveling to do. And be swift!","rew":"Money: 1 50 1 gold, 50 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,700\n+200 reputation with Stormwind","back":"‹name›! Do you have that haunch? I must begin preparing it soon, or the banquet will be ruined!","done":"Ah, this will do nicely! Many, many thanks!\nNow if you'll excuse me, I must get the haunch chopped, marinated and garnished for the banquet.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":51.8,"y":93.6,"n":"Angus Stern","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"932":{"id":932,"t":"Twisted Hatred","lv":8,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 8 instead of 7. Gives 700 experience instead of 625, 1.12 times as much. Partly read from what the game server sent.","obj":"Kill Lord Melenas and bring his head to Tallonkai Swiftroot in Dolanaar.\nMelenas' Head Lord Melenas","desc":"I must warn you, ‹name›, this matter must stay between us. The satyr are enough of an embarrassment to us already, and this one is much too close to home.\nHe is called Lord Melenas. He resides in the nearby cave of Fel Rock where he has gathered a large group of grell warriors. His heart is black as night, and he plots something most foul.\nYou must find him within his nearby cave just to the north of here, and bring me his head.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFeral Bracers Viny Wrappings\nExperience: 700\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Did you kill Lord Melenas yet? It is vital that he be taken care of quickly and quietly, ‹name›. His continued existence is an embarrassment to us all.","done":"With Lord Melenas laid to rest I can finally move on to other matters. Thank you, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":55.6,"y":56.9,"n":"Tallonkai Swiftroot","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"1492":{"id":1492,"t":"Wharfmaster Dizzywig","lv":11,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Secure Crate to Wharfmaster Dizzywig in Ratchet.\nSecure Crate\nProvided: Secure Crate","desc":"I have need to send a crate of potions, reagents and other items to my associates in the Old World. Little time I have to actually see them to the dock at Ratchet, and the last caravan has already left.\nIf you could, please take this to Wharfmaster Dizzywig. He will ensure that it is placed on the next boat to Blackwater Cove.","rew":"Experience: 440\n+50 reputation with Ratchet","back":"You seek passage on the next ship, or have some item you wish to send aboard it?","done":"A small enough crate. Yes, I should be able to find room for this aboard the ship. It sails with the next tide, I trust this is soon enough? Excellent. Let me just enter it into my ledger.\nAll taken care of! Good day to you, ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":51.4,"y":30.2,"n":"Apothecary Helbrim","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":63.4,"y":38.5,"n":"Wharfmaster Dizzywig","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"852":{"id":852,"t":"Hezrul Bloodmark","lv":19,"min":11,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Hezrul's Head to Regthar Deathgate, west of the Crossroads.\nHezrul's Head Hezrul Bloodmark","desc":"Hezrul Bloodmark is the leader of the Kolkar centaurs in the Barrens. He is fierce, brutal and cunning. Defeating him would disrupt and fracture the Kolkars, greatly reducing their threat to us.\nSo kill him. As with Barak and Verog, bring me Hezrul's Head.\nHe leads his people from the Lushwater Oasis, to the south.","rew":"You will receive:\nBounty Hunter's Ring\nMoney: 8 0 gold, 8 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,100\n+75 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Is Hezrul defeated, ‹name›?","done":"I commend you, ‹name›. These centaur are undisciplined and cannot focus their rage as the orcs can, but they are fierce nonetheless. In defeating them, your valor is proven.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":45.3,"y":28.4,"n":"Regthar Deathgate","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"2932":{"id":2932,"t":"Grim Message","lv":42,"min":35,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gather Witherbark Skulls and place on Nimboya's Pike. Place Nimboya's Laden Pike at one of the Witherbark Villages in the Hinterlands, then return to Nimboya in Stranglethorn.\nProvided: Nimboya's Pike","desc":"The Witherbark trolls were once allies to the Horde, but they betrayed Thrall... and that must be punished!\nHere, take my pike and go to the Hinterlands, far to the north. You will find it northeast of Tarren Mill, a village held by our allies, the Forsaken.\nWhen you enter the Hinterlands, hunt Witherbark trolls. Gather their skulls and drive my pike into the ground at one of their smaller villages, Hiri'watha or Zun'watha.\nShow them their vile actions are of consequence!","rew":"Money: 55 0 gold, 55 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,450\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"You have not completed my task, ‹name›.","done":"Word reached me of your deed. A grim deed, but one of honor. Let us hope the Witherbarks heed your message.\nStranglethorn Vale The Hinterlands","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":32.2,"y":27.7,"n":"Nimboya","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"372":{"id":372,"t":"At War With The Scarlet Crusade","lv":12,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Executor Zygand in the town of Brill wants you to assassinate Captain Melrache and his two bodyguards.\nCaptain Melrache slain\nScarlet Bodyguard slain : 0/ 2","desc":"Scarlet Crusaders have been raiding from the ruined tower in northern Tirisfal, past Faol's Rest. According to the information we have, a ruthless commander named Captain Melrache is in charge of this evil crew.\nI am entrusting you now with a special and dangerous mission. Slay Melrache and his two bodyguards, in the name of The Dark Lady.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCeremonial Knife Striking Hatchet\nExperience: 900\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"You have not yet performed your duty, ‹class›. We cannot expect to carry out The Dark Lady's plan with the Scarlet Crusade pestering our soldiers. Bring about their deaths and perform your duty to Sylvanas!","done":"You have done extremely well, ‹class›. With ruthless fighters like you conquering in the name of The Forsaken our race is one step closer to defeating Arthas once and for all. I have a good feeling about you, comrade.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":60.6,"y":51.8,"n":"Executor Zygand","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"4292":{"id":4292,"t":"The Bait for Lar'korwi","lv":56,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Using the contents of Torwa's Pouch, summon Lar'korwi and defeat him. Then bring Lar'korwi's Head to Torwa Pathfinder near the entrance to Un'Goro Crater.\nLar'korwi's Head Lar'korwi\nProvided: Torwa's Pouch","desc":"This will be the most difficult part because there is some complexity to the plan. To the north of here, you will find a small trail into the mountains. It was here I saw Lar'korwi last. You will know you are in the right area because of all the bones from massive creatures that once wandered nearby. Take the meat you recovered and place it there. Then, rub this mixture I created on the meat. If both lures mingled together do not bring Lar'korwi to you, then I know nothing else that will.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nPlainstalker Tunic Outrider Leggings\nExperience: 7,300","back":"Do not let fear overpower you, ‹name›. Fear is the great betrayer... you must remain strong!\nTake the meat, place it in the small valley, and then use the gland on it. Only then will death come for you.","done":"The Earth Mother be praised! You've done it! Fair play to you, ‹name›. You have proven to be a great ‹class› in your own right. Your spirit is strong. Your bravery unmatched. And your strength has been fortified. I bow down to your skills.\nOnly the greatest of my ancestors could have accomplished something so incredible. Congratulations.","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":71.6,"y":76,"n":"Torwa Pathfinder","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"92532":{"id":92532,"t":"The warriors path","lv":2,"min":2,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Read the Crumpled Note you've been given, then seek out Blademaster Ren inside the Thendal Village watchtower.\nProvided: Crumpled Note","desc":"While you were gone our warrior trainer--Blademaster Ren--requested that we send you their way when you returned. She dropped this note off for you as well.\nGive it a read, then find Blademaster Ren inside the village watchtower.","back":"So you've come for training, then?","done":"You are about to embark upon a dangerous journey. Our world is changing and it will need those who have the will to lead and protect others if our people hope to survive. As you grow in power you will need guidance. Come to me--I will do what I can to train you as you progress.\nGood luck, Zaelriel, may the winds guide you.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":42,"y":23.4,"n":"Rorian the Dayseeker","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":43.6,"y":24.2,"n":"Blademaster Ren","e":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"8372":{"id":8372,"t":"Fight for Warsong Gulch","lv":19,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Warsong Gulch Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"The Silverwing Sentinels are at war with the Warsong Outriders due to the destruction the Orcs are causing to the forest. There are, however, more reasons to defend this particular forest than plain love for nature.\nThe forest forms a strategic barrier that makes Ashenvale defendable against a large-scale attack. Without it, Astranaar would last a day or two before being annexed to the Barrens.\nDo your part in fighting the Warsong Outriders, ‹name›! For the Alliance!","rew":"Money: 11 0 gold, 11 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,450\n+100 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels","back":"You've come back with news from the front, ‹name›?","done":"Well done, ‹name›! You've served the Alliance well.\nDun Morogh Darnassus Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":35.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":58,"y":34.2,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":81.2,"y":38.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"5092":{"id":5092,"t":"Clear the Way","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 10 Skeletal Flayers and 10 Slavering Ghouls in Sorrow Hill.\nReturn to Commander Ashlam Valorfist at Chillwind Camp, Western Plaguelands.\nSkeletal Flayer slain : 0/ 10\nSlavering Ghoul slain : 0/ 10","desc":"With Andorhal's western and northern roads into the city well fortified, I'm looking to strike at it from the less defended eastern road. The Scourge relies on the buffer of undead that infests Sorrow Hill as a first line of defense. If we are to advance on Andorhal, we will need to do it through Sorrow Hill.\nYour first assignment will be to clear the way through Sorrow Hill. Thin out the skeletons and ghouls that haunt the area; report back to me when this is done!","rew":"Money: 75 0 gold, 75 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,100\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"I want you to prepare for the worst, ‹name› - dig deep. The task in front of us will not be easy. As we rally our forces here to eventually strike out against the Scourge, you will be part of our advance effort that takes the fight to them! Your assigned mission in Sorrow Hill will begin our path to victory!","done":"Mission accomplished, ‹name›! Well played, well played.\nAllow me to reward your work thus far with some coin from the Stormwind coffers. I'd recommend spending it on materiel that will aid you in your next mission... one that will take you into the ruins of Andorhal itself.\nBe ready! Be vigilant!","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":42.7,"y":84,"n":"Commander Ashlam Valorfist","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"132":{"id":132,"t":"The Defias Brotherhood","lv":18,"min":14,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take Wiley's Note to Gryan Stoutmantle in Westfall.\nWiley's Note\nProvided: Wiley's Note","desc":"What I am about to tell you could cost me my life. The Defias gang is up to something big. Last I heard they were working in conjunction with various gnolls, kobolds and even goblins.\nTake this note to Stoutmantle. It explains as much as I know on the subject.","rew":"Experience: 675\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Good to see you back, ‹name›. What did Wiley have to say for himself?","done":"Bah! I should have let that scoundrel rot when I had the chance. But this information is crucial. Good work.\nRedridge Mountains Westfall","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":21.4,"y":45.3,"n":"Wiley the Black","s":1},{"z":"Westfall","x":56.3,"y":47.5,"n":"Gryan Stoutmantle","e":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"292":{"id":292,"t":"The Eye of Paleth","lv":30,"min":22,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Cursed Eye of Paleth to Glorin Steelbrow.\nCursed Eye of Paleth\nProvided: Cursed Eye of Paleth","desc":"Opening the chest reveals a blackened orb, pulsing with an eerie light. It is the treasure of which Fitzsimmons spoke: a Cursed Eye of Paleth.\nTake the Cursed Eye of Paleth to the dwarven priest Glorin Steelbrow, in Menethil Harbor. Ask him how to remove the Eye's curse.","rew":"Experience: 1,200\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"That drunk Fitzsimmons sent you to me? Well, you can tell him I don't have any extra ale. He's going to have to panhandle someone else!","done":"An Eye of Paleth? Amazing! Hmm... there's something wrong with this one. You found it on one of those shipwrecks? Well that explains it! But... I didn't know they had such an Eye on the Third Fleet...\nIt's no wonder Fitzsimmons was so spooked. A Cursed Eye of Paleth is no cause for mirth.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":14.4,"y":24,"n":"Intrepid's Locked Strongbox","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":10.6,"y":60.6,"n":"Glorin Steelbrow","e":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"5252":{"id":5252,"t":"Remorseful Highborne","lv":58,"min":53,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Wynd Nightchaser in Starfall Village, and ask about the proper place for the Crystal of Zin-Malor.\nCrystal of Zin-Malor\nProvided: Crystal of Zin-Malor","desc":"The... the crystal...\nThe highborne here are clouded by their own misssery...\nI am sorrrrrowful, but I realize the errorrrr of what happened so long ago. Even though there is no waaaay to change the past, I am now at peacccce knowing that you have recovered the crystal of Zin-Malor...\nYouuu must return it...\nIt muuuussst be returrrned.","rew":"Experience: 4,650\n+25 reputation with Alliance","back":"It has been some time since you left, ‹name›. How have you fared?","done":"Is that... what I think it is?","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":56.1,"y":44.4,"n":"Remorseful Highborne","s":1},{"z":"Winterspring","x":52,"y":30.4,"n":"Wynd Nightchaser","e":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"93172":{"id":93172,"t":"Free the hollows","lv":13,"min":8,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Destroy 10 Wind Hollows in Shadowgale Forest.\nWind Hollow freed : 0/ 10","desc":"Most of the elves on this island seem to think that these woods are haunted, and they aren't wrong.\nAt the old ruins to the northeast, a strange type of ghost-like spirits gather. Some nights, you can almost hear them \"singing\". It's not like any song I've heard before, but its definitely a song and its... just so sad.\nI'm not sure why, but I think something terrible happened there at some point, and the spirits are trapped there somehow. If you are feeling brave, maybe you can help set them free?","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFreedom Walkers Sorrowsong Gloves Scuffed Cuffs\nExperience: 675","back":"We can only hope that those poor spirits are able to find peace after being freed from this place.","done":"Thank you, stranger.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":54,"y":39,"n":"Strange Hermit","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"8052":{"id":8052,"t":"The All-Seeing Eye of Zuldazar","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","obj":"The Eye of Zuldazar","rew":"You will receive:\nThe All-Seeing Eye of Zuldazar\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"If only we had ten-thousand more like you, ‹name›. The armies of Hakkar would be scattered to the wind in the blink of an eye.\n<Al'tabim sighs.>\nAlas, the Eye is ready to realize its full potential. Give it to me.","done":"Smite them all and let Hakkar sort them out...","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16.1,"n":"Al'tabim the All-Seeing","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]}});